all 1: Create my components (Secondary Button, Back Button, Section Header ×2, Stock Row ×7, Index Card ×2? (instances with overrides instead — one component, 2 instances), Tab Bar ×3, Numpad Key + Number Pad, Code Box, Payment Option ×2, List Row, Stat Card). Return created IDs.\n2. Build call 2: Frames 01_Splash, 02_Onboarding, 06_Welcome.\n3. Build call 3: Frames 03_Empty, 03_Filled, 04_Verify_Phone, 05_Verify_Code.\n4. Build call 4: Frame 07_Home.\n5. Build call 5: Frames 08_Portfolio, 09_Stock_Detail.\n6. Build call 6: Frames 10_Confirm_Order, 11_Profile.\n7. Build call 7: prototype wiring (all reactions).\n8. Screenshots batched in parallel calls (get_screenshot supports one node each; I can issue multiple parallel calls in one block).\n9. Fixes.\n\nEach use_figma ≤50000 chars — plenty.\n\nFonts: load Inter Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold at start of each build call.\n\nComponent creation details — I'll write helpers inside each call (functions can't persist across calls; each call is isolated JS). Repeated helper code per call is fine.\n\nText creation helper:\n```js\nfunction T(parent, chars, size, style, hex, x, y, opts={}) {\n  const t = figma.createText();\n  t.fontName = {family:'Inter', style};\n  t.characters = chars; t.fontSize = size;\n  t.fills = [solid(hex)];\n  parent.appendChild(t); t.x=x; t.y=y;\n  if (opts.w) { t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(opts.w, t.height); }\n  if (opts.align) t.textAlignHorizontal = opts.align;\n  return t;\n}\n```\nMust await figma.loadFontAsync for each style before setting fontName.\n\nsolid(hex): {type:'SOLID', color: hexToRgb}.\n\nRounded rect helper: figma.createRectangle + cornerRadius.\n\nFrame helper: createFrame, resize, fills, cornerRadius.\n\nVector path helper for sparklines:\n```js\nfunction spark(parent, pts, color, x, y, w, h, weight=2) {\n  const v = figma.createVector();\n  const d = pts.map((p,i)=>(i? 'L':'M')+' '+p[0]+' '+p[1]).join(' ');\n  v.vectorPaths = [{windingRule:'NONE', data: d}];\n```\nwindingRule for open stroke paths: 'NONE' is valid. v.strokes=[solid(color)]; v.strokeWeight=2; v.strokeCap='ROUND'; v.strokeJoin='ROUND'; v.fills=[]; then position x,y. Note: vectorPaths coordinates start at 0,0; resize? The vector's size auto-computes from path bounds? Setting vectorPaths defines geometry; node size adjusts? Actually after setting vectorPaths, the node bounds may not auto-fit; need v.resize(w,h)? Hmm — setting vectorPaths: the vector network is set; node width/height update to path bounding box I believe. Then set x,y. Stroke extends beyond bounds visually — fine.\n\nLine/area chart for portfolio: area fill needs closed path with brand 10% fill + stroke path. Two vectors.\n\nLet me also handle the eye icon on portfolio card (Icon_Balance_Visibility instance 24×19.2).\n\nTab bar component: 375×56 white, top border (1px #E6E8F0 line). 5 tabs evenly at width 75: Home x=0..75 etc. Icon 24 + label 10. Center Trade: brand circle 44×44 at x=165.5, y=-10? Floating style — circle centered y 6, label \"Trade\" below? Floating elevated circle: circle center at top edge overlapping. Simpler inline: all 5 inline; Trade icon white on brand circle 40×40 (circle centered in tab). Label \"Trade\" below circle 10px. Active tab color brand; Trade always brand circle (it's an action). Market inactive gray.\nVariants: property \"Active\" = Home/Portfolio/Profile. In each variant, corresponding icon+label brand, others #9AA0B4.\n\nWait — Icon_Trade white on brand circle: good. Other icons are black vectors presumably → override fills to gray/brand per state. Icons inside instances: override child fills — allowed. I'll write helper `tint(node, hex)` that sets fills on all vector/text children recursively (skipping groups; groups have no fills).\n\nHome indicator: instance on every frame at y=778. On dark splash: white fill instance → override fills=[] and child rect to white.\n\nStatus bar: white bg instance. On splash: fills=[] + children tinted white. On others: fills=[] (transparent, screen bg shows) — text black fine. StatusBar has frames \"Signal\"/\"Battery\" with fills [] containing shapes — tinting recursively ALL descendants to white/black: careful not to tint empty frames' fills ([] already). I'll tint only nodes with visible solid fills.\n\nNumpad: component 327×264? Keys 105×52 gap 6: 3×105+2×6=327 ✓. 4 rows: 4×52+3×8=232. Component 327×232. Keys: white fill, radius 12, digit 22 Medium text1 centered; '*' 22; '0'; delete key: white with backspace vector. Instances on 04/05. No interactions needed (entry only? Number pad isn't in links; fine, no links on keys).\n\nCode Box: 56×56 white radius 12 border 1.5 #E6E8F0; digit text centered 24 SemiBold. Instance overrides: text chars + border color for filled box.\n\nPayment Option: 327×76 white radius 12 border; icon 40 area; title 15 SemiBold; sub 12 text2; radio right 20×20 circle border 1.5 text3. Variants Card / Apple Pay with respective icons (Icon_Card 24×18.5, Icon_Apple_Pay 21×24).\n\nList Row: 327×52; label 15 Medium text1 left x=16; value right (text2 14) + chevron \">\" vector right. Variants? One component; instances override label/value; FAQ/others no value → hide value text (visible=false).\n\nSection Header: 327×24: title 17 SemiBold text1; variant \"Add\": plus circle button 24 right (brand).\n\nStock Row variant structure (327×56): white radius 14? Rows as white cards on bg. Children: logo frame 36×36 (logo instance inside centered), ticker 15 SemiBold, company 12 text2 (below ticker), price 15 SemiBold right-ish x≈228, change 13 Medium colored right-aligned, sparkline 56×20 right at x≈260? Layout: [logo 36] [ticker/company stacked x=52] ... [sparkline x=205 w=56] [price/change stacked right-aligned x=268 w=47]. Price right aligned. Change colored.\nFor wishlist variants (AMZN, ADBE): include price too (hide on Home via visibility). FB variant reused in both.\n\nChange color: green #16A34A for +, red #DC2626 for −. F: −0.32% red; AMZN −0.05% red.\n\nSparkline