e workspace page too (allowed) — maybe a \"Components\" section at y=−600 or to the right at x=1900. Components on workspace page: allowed (\"New frames, reusable components and prototype connections are allowed in this workspace\").\n\nComponent set creation: figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, parent) — creates ComponentSetNode. Variant naming: node.name = \"Active=Home\" etc. Let me use combineAsVariants for Stock Row (Property: Stock=...) and Tab Bar (Active=...), Payment Option (Type=...), Section Header (Style=Plain/Add).\n\nText auto-resize: default textAutoResize is WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT. For centered multi-line subtitle: set width + textAlignHorizontal CENTER + textAutoResize HEIGHT.\n\nAlso set all frames clipsContent = true.\n\nLet me now write Build Call 1: components. This is the biggest code. I'll structure it carefully. I'll return JSON of created component IDs for later reference. I must store IDs to create instances in later calls — I can find them by name via figma.currentPage.findChild or figma.getLocalComponents? In later calls: figma.currentPage.findOne(n => n.name === 'Stock Row' && n.type==='COMPONENT_SET')? Components created on page 5:2. findOne by name works. Also given components by ID (4:168 etc.) directly.\n\nActually, simpler: in each subsequent call, `const comps = figma.getPageByIdAsync('5:2')... findAll(n => n.type==='COMPONENT' || n.type==='COMPONENT_SET')` and index by name. Fine.\n\nVariant detail: for combineAsVariants, nodes must be ComponentNodes with names \"Prop=Value\". The set node gets placed where? combineAsVariants(nodes, parent, index) — parent = page. Position set node manually.\n\nInstances from variants: setVariant.createInstance() creates default variant instance; to pick variant: inst.setProperties({'Stock': 'NFLX'}) or setProperties({variantName...}). Property name = \"Stock\". I'll use setProperties({'Active=Home'... }) hmm — componentPropertyDefinitions on set: for variants, property name e.g. \"Active\", values [\"Home\"