{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key finding: reactions validation error — \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'overlay' at [0].action\". So the action schema does NOT accept 'overlay' key. Need action: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null} without overlay. And for AFTER_DELAY trigger, error was only about overlay in action — so trigger AFTER_DELAY with timeout is probably fine once action is fixed!\n\nThe 4 screens built successfully (fE 17 children, fF 17, f04 8, f05 12), but ALL link() calls failed due to overlay key. Next call: re-wire all failed links + splash delay, using action without 'overlay'.\n\nLinks to set now:\n- f01 (11:110) AFTER_DELAY 1500 → 11:111\n- fF Continue button (last created btn in fF) → 11:114\n- f04 back → 11:113; f04 Send code → 11:115\n- f05 back → 11:114; f05 Verify → 11:116\n\nI'll find nodes by traversal: in fF, the button instance = findOne(n=>n.type==='INSTANCE'&&n.componentId==='4:168'... hmm mainComponent id. Simpler: fF.findOne(n=>n.type==='INSTANCE'&&n.name==='Button') — component name is probably 'Button'. Let me instead find by: fF.children.filter(c=>c.type==='INSTANCE') and match size 327×52. For f04: back = instance 40×40; send = 327×52. f05 same.\n\nAlso onboarding 02 (11:111): Sign up→03E, Skip→03E — wait summary says Skip→03_Empty? \"Sign up→03_Empty, Skip→03_Empty\". Yes both → 03E (11:112). Need to set those too. Find in 11:111: the Sign up button = instance 327×52 at y=640; Skip = text 'Skip'. Set reactions on text node works? Reactions can be set on any scene node. Text nodes support reactions (hotspot area = text bounds). OK.\n\nWelcome (11:116): CTA \"I'm ready to start!\" → 07 (11:117). Button instance in f06.\n\nDo all in one wiring call with the fixed action shape. Return read-back of each node's reactions to verify.","signature":"b62850c3860c4ed79be31589"}],"id":"22796094-d90b-4c0d-b5a2-b6c532c5c94e","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","