{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"08_Portfolio issues:\n1. Chart line: the line goes BELOW the card and gets clipped — line starts at (20,150) which is bottom of plot, fine, but looking at screenshot the line dips below card at left edge... Actually the line looks cut off at the bottom-left corner (starts at Mon y=150 = card local 150, card height 196 → y=150 is inside). Hmm the visible issue: the line exits the card at bottom-left — because the area fill's closing edge (L 307 150 L 20 150 Z) draws along y=150, but the LINE vector (unclosed) starts at 20,150 — inside. But screenshot shows line crossing the card's bottom edge near x=0..20 — wait, the line seems to start at card's left edge around y=325 abs (local ~101?) Hmm.\n\nLook again: line visible from bottom-left corner rising to Tue peak ~y=262 abs... The area fill also extends below the line's end? The area bottom is clipped by card. What's odd: the line's Mon point at (20,150) local → abs (44,374). Card spans abs y=224..420. So 374 is inside. In the screenshot the blue line at bottom-left touches y≈330/812*812... let me not over-analyze pixel positions; the shape looks like: line from bottom-left (44,374 abs) up to Tue (92,304)... screenshot shows peak at ~(70,265)?? \n\nActually bigger visible issue: the LINE only shows as partial segments — from x≈0 (card edge!) rising. The line appears to START at the card's left edge below the chart area (y≈330 abs = local ~106?). Hmm wait: could the vector's x/y have been auto-set to bounding box (0,0 is path min?) — V() sets v.x=0,v.y=0 THEN no resize for line (only spark resizes). vectorPaths data uses absolute coords 20..307/40..150; v.x=0,v.y=0 → path renders at its data coords relative to node position (0,0 of card). Correct.\n\nHmm but screenshot: there IS a line segment near bottom-left going below the area fill... The area fill (light blue) ends at y=150 local = abs 374. Below that, the line continues to... no.\n\nOK let me