t node origin.\n\nSo fix: after creating the line/area vectors, set v.x=20, v.y=40 (path bounds min) — i.e., set node.x = minX of path data, node.y = minY. For portfolio: x=20, y=40. For detail chart: x=20, y=30. The area fills share same bounds (min y=40/30) — area bounds min y = min(cy)=40 → x=20,y=40. Detail: min py=30 → x=20,y=30.\n\nWait but then in the SPLASH/02 minis the sparks: spark() sets v.x=x passed, v.y=y passed — those match intended placement since resize keeps normalized geometry at node origin → correct. And they rendered correctly ✓ (07 spark looked right). Good — consistent.\n\nSo in 08: area v.x=20,v.y=40; line v.x=20,v.y=40; dot at (303,36) — dot was positioned absolutely (303,36) with ellipse — correct in screenshot? Screenshot shows dot at right ~(345 abs, 290)... the chip is at right with dot right of it — dot visible near 'Sun' chip at top right ✓ (positioned by absolute coords, ellipses don't normalize). Chip fine.\n\nBut wait — in 08 the chip overlaps the line at top right. Chip at (190,30) local, w=113 → 190..303; dot at 303..311. Line passes y≈50-62 in that x range → chip at y=30..52 overlaps line slightly. Screenshot shows chip overlapping the line a bit — acceptable, but nudge chip to (188,24)? Line at x=211 is y=50 → chip bottom 52 touches. Slightly raise: y=22. OK.\n\n2. x labels (Mon..Sun) are TOO LOW/faded? They're at y=160 local → abs 384, inside card (ends 420) ✓ visible in screenshot ✓. Fine.\n\n3. Everything else (value card, stat cards, rows, tab bar Portfolio active) looks great.\n\nNow 09 check.","signature":"05e80d6fbace460cafab7a9f"}],"id":"9147ac5e-97ff-42b8-a346-5426789b482d","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c973adbc-afb1-4b2b-9729-fe67e5204bf5","uuid":"d2379e20-0501-4888-884e-25ae40841e66","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:29:39.250Z","thinking_durati