eight — need to know current geometry. From build: card at (24, ~... ) rows every 36px: Funding 230?, ... Total at y=?? The Total text is clipped at card bottom. Card height needs +28 or move Total up. I need actual node geometry — I'll query in the fix call: find the card frame containing 'Total' text and its height; find Total text y. Fix: card.resize(w, totalY+20-cardY) roughly, or just +30 height.\n\nFor the bell/eye icons: inspect component structure first. Let me do a read-only inspection call for: 3:155 (Icon_Notifications), 3:143 (Icon_Balance_Visibility) structure — children types, fills, strokes. Also for 10: find summary card + Total text geometry. Also 03E/03F: confirm current positions of 'GIcon' and apple vector. And measure natural widths of 'Continue with Google'/'Continue with Apple' at 16 Semi Bold.\n\nI can do all inspection in one use_figma call (read-only, no writes — but the tool is transactional; a read-only call is fine).\n\nThen a single fix call. Let me write the inspection call.\n\nActually, to save calls: inspection + fixes could be one call if I compute everything inside. The icon fix logic: inspect structure at runtime and apply targeted recolor:\n- For Icon_Notifications instance: for each descendant node: if it has strokes (array with SOLID) → set strokes=[S(t1)]; if fills has SOLID and NOT strokes → hmm. Risk: bell shape might be filled (filled bell) rather than stroked. If component = filled bell shape + white bg circle, then tint() made both dark → solid square. Targeted fix: set the bg (likely first child / RECTANGLE or ELLIPSE with fills) to fills=[] or white, and the bell vector to t1.\n\nI can't know without inspecting. Do inspection first (read-only), then fix. Two calls. Also measure label widths in the inspection call via temp text nodes (create, measure, remove — creates changes but harmless; keep it in inspection call since it's non-destructive... actually creating/removing temp nodes is a write-ish op but fine in a \"read