ws\nconst f07=await get('11:117');\nout.f07rows=f07.children.filter(n=>n.name.startsWith('Stock Row')||n.name.includes('Section')).map(n=>({name:n.name,x:n.x,y:n.y}));\nconst f08=await get('11:118');\nout.f08vec=f08.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR').map(n=>({name:n.name,x:n.x,y:n.y,w:n.width,h:n.height}));\nconst f09=await get('11:119');\nout.f09vec=f09.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR').map(n=>({name:n.name,x:n.x,y:n.y,w:n.width,h:n.height}));\nreturn out;\n```\n\nHmm — vectors inside instances: findAll includes instance children but I can't set fills on instance children (they're read-only overrides except text/fills?). Vector position inside instance can't be changed. The chart vectors I created are plain vectors in the frame (not instances) — find them by being direct frame children or by name. My spark/area/line vectors: did I name them? spark() doesn't set name; V() doesn't set name. They'll have default names like \"Vector\". findAll(type==='VECTOR') catches them plus any vector children inside component instances (which I can't move). To be safe, in the fix call I'll filter to vectors whose parent is the frame itself or a plain frame (not INSTANCE), and skip those inside instances (n.findOne chain: check ancestor types).\n\nBetter: in fix call, get frame children that are VECTOR directly (the line/area were appended directly to chart card frame — I created a card frame F() and appended area/line to it). So: cardFrame.children.filter(type==='VECTOR'). I'll locate by name 'ChartCard' if I named it... I used o.name maybe. Safer: find frames with height>100 containing VECTOR children in f08: the chart card. Just do: const cards=f08.children.filter(n=>n.type==='FRAME'); then for each, vecs=card.children.filter(v=>v.type==='VECTOR'). The portfolio chart card is the one with 2 vectors (area+line). For f09: chart card has area+line = 2 vectors; the chevrons/back arrow vector is Back Button instance child (inside instance, skip). Bars are RECTANGLES. So filter vectors whose parent is a direct FRAME child of the main frame.\n\nOK let me write inspection now.","signature":"85deabfd1a5e4852b1c33cfa"}],"id":"9af8306b-e13e-4f18-9aaa-ca25d366e35e","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c973adbc-afb1-4b2b-9729-fe67e5204bf5","uuid":"6310a24c-ac19-4956-887c-f34cebb68c0c","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:34:14.900Z","thinking_duration_ms":47066}
